  "Question": "A rectangular field is half as wide as it is long and is completely enclosed by \\(x\\) yards of fencing. The area in terms of \\(x\\) is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac{x^2}{2}\\)",
    "B": "\\(2x^2\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac{2x^2}{9}\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac{x^2}{18}\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\dfrac{x^2}{72}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Let the width be \\(w>0\\) yards. Since the field is half as wide as it is long, its length is \\(2w\\) yards. The fencing covers the entire perimeter, so\n\\[\nx=2(w+2w)=6w.\n\\]\nHence the width is \\(x/6\\) and the length is \\(x/3\\). Multiplying length by width gives the area:\n\\[\n\\frac{x}{3}\\cdot\\frac{x}{6}\n=\\boxed{\\frac{x^2}{18}}\\text{ square yards}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice \\(\\boxed{D}\\).",
